Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: bucklespring
Source: https://github.com/barak/bucklespring
Comment: The project began at https://github.com/zevv/bucklespring, which is
 where every release up to 1.5.1 came from; the 2.x releases are made from
 the repository above, which is what debian/watch follows.

Files: *
Copyright: 2016-2025 Ico Doornekamp <ico@zevv.nl>
License: GPL-2+

Files: scan-mac.c
Copyright: 2016-2025 Ico Doornekamp <ico@zevv.nl>
License: GPL-2+
Comment: The table mapping Mac virtual keycodes to set-1 scancodes is taken
 from VirtualBox,
 https://www.virtualbox.org/svn/vbox/trunk/src/VBox/Frontends/VirtualBox/src/platform/darwin/DarwinKeyboard.cpp
 and the event tap callback is adapted from
 https://danielbeard.wordpress.com/2010/10/29/listening-for-global-keypresses-in-osx/
 .
 This file is only compiled on macOS; it is not built by, or shipped in,
 any of the Debian binary packages.

Files: configure.ac
       Makefile.am
       tray.c
       wl-repeat.c
       tools/make-clips.py
       systemd/*
       udev/*
Copyright: 2026 Barak A. Pearlmutter <barak@pearlmutter.net>
License: GPL-2+
Comment: The build system, the system tray icon, the Wayland repeat rate
 query, the systemd user units and the uaccess udev rule began as Debian
 packaging and have since moved upstream.

Files: tests/*
Copyright: 2026 David Csiki <csdivad@gmail.com>
License: GPL-2+
Comment: The test for the libinput flavour's login session handling, from
 the fork where that handling was written.

Files: man/*
Copyright: 2016-2025 Ico Doornekamp <ico@zevv.nl>
           2016-2017 Dominik George <nik@naturalnet.de>
           2026 Barak A. Pearlmutter <bap@debian.org>
License: GPL-2+
Comment: The pages for the executables are generated from their own --help
 and --version output by help2man(1), so the option list and the AUTHOR and
 COPYRIGHT sections of each page are that program's text; the prose around
 them, in the matching .h2m include files, was first written for the Debian
 package by Dominik George.

Files: clips/bucklespring/*
Copyright: 2016-2025 Ico Doornekamp <ico@zevv.nl>
License: GPL-2+
Comment: The IBM Model M recordings the program began with, transcoded from
 wav to FLAC without loss.

Files: clips/vain-qwertz/*
Copyright: 2017 vain <vain@uninformativ.de>
License: GPL-2+
Comment: A full QWERTZ layout with two to four takes of every key,
 contributed to the upstream project through its pull requests and carried
 on its samplesets branch; transcoded from wav to FLAC without loss.

Files: clips/sequential/*
Copyright: 2025 SequentialDesign <https://github.com/SequentialDesign>
License: GPL-2+
Comment: Recorded on a fork of this project and offered through its pull
 request 135, under no terms of their own, so taken under the project's;
 transcoded from wav to FLAC without loss.

Files: clips/beeper/*
Copyright: 2020 mejs <https://github.com/mejs>
License: GPL-2+
Comment: The single beep of the beepykeyboard fork, for a Model M with its
 PC speaker wired up.  Recorded on a fork of this project under no terms of
 its own, so taken under the project's; transcoded without loss.

Files: clips/drums/*
       clips/piano/*
       clips/slapstick/*
Copyright: 2026 Barak A. Pearlmutter <bap@debian.org>
License: GPL-2+
Comment: Entirely synthesised by tools/make-clips.py, which is in the
 source and can regenerate them.

